<description>&lt;p&gt;Libyan armed forces continue extrajudicial executions and hold dozens of detainees at risk of execution, while Haftar's forces have signed a strategic cooperation protocol with Niger. An armed group closed the crude valve feeding the Zawiya refinery, disrupting oil supplies. A Christian was killed by Islamic State after refusing to renounce Jesus, and a study mapped tuberculosis cases in southern Libya. The Libyan Ministry of Justice affirmed its branches' commitment to improving the justice system across regions, and MiG-29 aircraft were displayed with pilots. 2 battle-related deaths were recorded in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivgFBVV95cUxOVjFWejNpZjAwc0puNlJiS3NGQTZuazVna0hBQkxjcGdyTzVVLXJuVS1DbHY3cFVVZ3JubUNLNWhBLXJmUFl4TGVwRzFLSnZYajFYUWl3MzlGTXBDTXlqbGpENFRKWnpra3owZGJUSHM4M21LV2xJQzJMTnRsWDdkYVZKQmVHT2pQSGwyTFVlbDVjTFozM3JsYlVkSDkxbkVGaEVVYVVTdmxCOGhCdUlCM0E2d1ZhQjF6aTFOTnBB?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivgFBVV95cUxNWTEtRW9rNXQ2eDdSOVN0czJ3c3prOE05M1ZxdlhfSzh0TktTRE04cjNzdXNSZ1d2Ung1TW1BV3NBRFlZcFg3SF9qT21VcUJKRzVFRWxKSzhkcXJpWXNvRlFtQXhfZ1QyQlU1VEEyX1dpWHdhMV94c2dTeDhCb2VlZC1ScncwTUlTZG1TU1R5R1N4cTFmODhZQktFektPSXB2QlZkN205bGF6X0xwU3lRaUhLZDhIRUtNSjlaM3R3?oc=5&quot;&gt;Premier Christian News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiiwFBVV95cUxNVkFIeDB1QU5RakhSOVFNMllHUTVBQzExOGZtQ214OUNDdWdUdGs1Z2RGb3NFVXcxSUk3SjVPZElwWVpXd2RJQVRTWjRkU3lWZWd6RlctS3RLbUZDaUo4ZzVUM25lazZNLW02eUpGRm9FckVOMjUtaGNvZjVSSVo5RjlGdFVLNnJIUkVN?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Libya Observer&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;InfoMigrants&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Devdiscourse&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot